## Lessons from supersob's Approach

Traders studying supersob's track record can extract several principles worth considering. First, win rate is not destiny. A 50% success rate sounds unremarkable until you realize that nearly three million dollars in profit has been generated from it. What matters is the asymmetry between gains and losses, not the raw frequency of wins. Second, concentration can be a feature rather than a bug. By trading just eleven markets rather than spreading attention across hundreds, supersob has presumably developed deeper conviction in each position, enabling the kind of aggressive sizing that drives outsized returns. Third, volume itself can be a signal of confidence. When a trader consistently moves size on [Polymarket](https://polymarket.com/?r=POLYTips), it suggests they have done the work to justify that exposure. Watching where high-volume traders deploy capital can provide useful information for others trying to identify mispriced markets.

